Description: Add empty autocomplete field to base pagination response.
.
The Go client binary (compiled against the full OpenAPI schema) requires the
"autocomplete" property on all paginated API responses. This property is
normally provided by the enterprise AutocompletePagination class
(authentik/enterprise/search/pagination.py), which is removed in our OSS build.
.
Starting in 2025.12.2, the Go API client was regenerated with OpenAPI Generator
7.19.0 (upgraded from 6.2.0), which adds strict UnmarshalJSON methods that
validate all required properties. Without this patch, every paginated API call
from the Go binary fails with:
  "no value given for required property autocomplete"
.
This breaks the embedded outpost initialization (OutpostsInstancesList) and
brand/TLS routing (CoreBrandsList), causing /outpost.goauthentik.io/ping to
return 404.
.
The fix adds an empty "autocomplete": {} to the base Pagination response and
updates the schema to declare it as required, matching the OpenAPI spec.
.
Author: Matthew Ramirez <matthew.ramirez@chainguard.dev>
Forwarded: not-needed

diff --git a/authentik/api/pagination.py b/authentik/api/pagination.py
index b259920..ede5f61 100644
--- a/authentik/api/pagination.py
+++ b/authentik/api/pagination.py
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@ class Pagination(pagination.PageNumberPagination):
                     "end_index": self.page.end_index(),
                 },
                 "results": data,
+                "autocomplete": {},
             }
         )
 
@@ -47,8 +48,9 @@ class Pagination(pagination.PageNumberPagination):
             properties={
                 "pagination": PAGINATION.ref,
                 "results": schema,
+                "autocomplete": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {}},
             },
-            required=["pagination", "results"],
+            required=["pagination", "results", "autocomplete"],
         )
 
 
